      ],
      "source": "https://emke.uwm.edu/entry/village-of-river-hills/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1930, residents incorporated River Hills, enacting zoning that required one‑acre lots and banned commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Hills%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "River Hills is the only 100‑percent residential community in Milwaukee County, with 85 % of lots over five acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Hills%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between 1956 and 1971, a Nike missile silo stood on the village’s grounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
